lisa-design:
- Globs are compiled to anchored RE2 on the standard library (no gobwas/glob: extra dependency, unmaintained); `[...]` is literal; nested {} supported; fuzzed Compile never panics.
- Matching is case-sensitive; empty strings/lists, invalid UTF-8, empty re: and trailing \ are PatternErrors; nil Pattern / unset StringOrList = match anything.
- Model choice: exact prefer entry > earliest request-list element > agent default (HarnessOffer.defaultModel) > highest version (numeric dash/dot groups) > smallest id.
- Effort: earliest request-list element > medium if candidate > first in agent order; Resolve works on normalised efforts, adapters map them (EffortMapping).
- Subsumes takes the known model ids explicitly; duplicate harness names in harness.allowed are a catalog error (CAT804, CORE-S1-T03).

